&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Invisible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a generalist People Experience role. You&#39;ll work across the whole People team, taking things from idea to delivered, reporting to the People Experience Director as their main support for execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A good part of the job is making the rest of the team better at what it does: streamlining People Operations processes, rewriting the policies behind them, and getting their projects over the line. The rest is content, programs, and employee relations casework of your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have proper support around you. In-house legal counsel covers anything with real risk attached, and our People Operations specialists own the systems and transactional work. Your job is improving how it all runs, not carrying it alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content:&lt;/strong&gt; you write the competency frameworks, policies, guides, and comms the team needs and never has time to produce properly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programs:&lt;/strong&gt; you run projects end to end. You build the plan, chase the stakeholders, hold the dates, and get it across the line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; you run and manage cases yourself, start to finish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and policy:&lt;/strong&gt; you find what&#39;s clunky across the People team and fix it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Content creation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write competency frameworks, career paths, and leveling content for teams across Invisible, working from subject matter input from leaders and business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain policies. Own the handbook. Keep it accurate as we change entities, countries, and structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft internal comms for People team initiatives: announcements, manager guidance, FAQs, rollout messaging. You&#39;ll write in our voice, which is direct and short. Not corporate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the practical stuff that makes a program real: manager toolkits, training decks, process guides, templates, briefing docs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Program management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate People team programs end to end: performance cycles, engagement survey and action planning, onboarding improvements, platform rollouts, framework launches, compliance projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build project plans with owners, dates, and dependencies. Track them. Escalate early when something slips.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate stakeholders across People, Legal, Finance, Talent Acquisition, and business leadership. They don&#39;t report to you and all of them are busy. You still get the decisions you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the follow-through after decisions get made. The gap between &quot;we agreed this&quot; and &quot;this is live&quot; is your job to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Employee Relations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and manage ER cases: grievances, investigations, performance management, absence, conduct, exits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take cases from intake to outcome. Hold meetings, take notes, gather evidence, write up findings, draft outcome letters, keep records clean.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our in-house employment counsel and the Employment Relations team on anything complex or high risk. You&#39;re supported on the hard ones, and you&#39;re running the caseload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot patterns. If three cases in one team say the same thing, you say so.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Supporting People Operations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the processes behind our day-to-day: onboarding and offboarding, contract changes, leave, reference letters, ticket flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document what isn&#39;t documented and simplify what&#39;s grown complicated. If a process you just ran was painful, you rewrite it before the next cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help People Ops land their projects: system rollouts, audit and compliance prep, vendor changes, data cleanups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull and sanity-check data when someone needs a number to make a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You use AI to produce content fast and well.&lt;/strong&gt; You can take a messy brief and a few stakeholder conversations and come back with a framework or policy that is accurate, readable, and on tone. We care about the output and the judgment behind it, not how long it took.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US employee relations case management. Essential.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve run US cases independently, including investigations and performance exits. You know where the legal risk sits, how it shifts by state, and when to escalate. Exposure to other jurisdictions is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A generalist track record in fast growth.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve worked in a generalist People or HR role at a startup or scale-up where the process didn&#39;t exist yet, and you were the person who actually delivered. You know what to build now and what can wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You finish things.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve project managed something with more than five stakeholders and landed it on time. You close the loop without being chased, and you flag risk early rather than explaining a miss afterward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You move people without authority.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll chase senior stakeholders for input and decisions. You&#39;re comfortable being politely relentless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re organized in a way other people can see.&lt;/strong&gt; Trackers, clear status, no surprises. If a program has six workstreams, you can tell us in 30 seconds where all six are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt; Some briefs will be clear. Some will be a sentence and a deadline. You come back with a draft, not a list of questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; HRIS, spreadsheets, survey data. You can pull the numbers, sanity-check them, and put them in front of someone who needs to decide something.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed org experience.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re global and remote-first, across multiple time zones and entities. You know how to keep things moving asynchronously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You like breadth.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;d rather do eight different things well than one thing forever, and you believe in evidence over instinct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re less interested in years of experience than in evidence you&#39;ve produced a lot of good work. Bring examples. Frameworks you wrote, programs you ran, cases you closed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$126,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$148,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It&#39;s Like to Work at Invisible:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Invisible, we’re not just redefining work—we’re reinventing it. We operate at the intersection of advanced AI and human ingenuity, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to unlock productivity and scale. Ownership is at the core of everything we do. Here, you won’t just execute tasks—you’ll build, innovate, and shape the future alongside world-class clients pushing the boundaries of AI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We expect bold ideas, relentless drive, and the ability to turn ambiguity into opportunity. The pace is fast, the challenges are big, and the growth is unmatched. We’re not for everyone, and we’re okay with that. If you’re looking for predictable routines, this isn’t the place for you. But if you’re driven to create, thrive in dynamic environments, and want a front-row seat to the AI revolution, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;Invisible is a hybrid organization with offices and team members located around the world. While some roles may offer remote flexibility, most positions involve in-office collaboration and are tied to specific locations. Any location-based requirements or hybrid expectations will be communicated by our Talent Acquisition team during the recruiting process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;AI Interviewing Guidelines:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Our hiring team thoughtfully uses AI to support an efficient, engaging, and inclusive interview process. Since AI can also be a helpful tool for candidates, we&#39;ve outlined expectations for using it ethically throughout your interview journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Click here to learn more about how we use AI and our guidelines for candidates.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accessibility Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(52, 73, 94);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for individuals with disabilities. If you require an accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please submit your request using our &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation request form.&lt;/a&gt; A member of our team will follow up to support your request.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Invisible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is an Applied AI research company closing the gap between frontier models and the enterprise. We provide the platform infrastructure that makes AI work in production at scale: unify fragmented data, map complex processes, orchestrate and evaluate agents, and stand up hyper-personalized workflow applications fast for companies like Grubhub, Alliance Global, and Thomson Reuters. Where models fall short, we build RL environments and data to fix them. The result: a virtuous cycle between enterprise deployment and model training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized as Best Predictive Analytics Platform of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards, Invisible makes AI work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Staffing Associate at Invisible Technologies gets qualified experts onto client projects and billing fast. Working with the Sr. Manager, Staffing, you&#39;ll turn client demand into staffed, productive teams: sourcing and vetting contractors, matching them to the right engagement, and moving them through onboarding to their first billed client hour. Demand shifts quickly, and projects often need to be staffed in days, not weeks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a 6-month, 40-hour-per-week contract with real potential to extend or convert. It suits a seasoned, agency-trained staffing professional who measures success in fill rates and billed hours, thrives on urgency, and wants to make an immediate impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff client projects end to end, turning incoming client demand into qualified contractors who are onboarded and billing hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with delivery and operations leads to understand each project&#39;s skill, volume and timeline needs, then build a staffing plan to meet them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source high volumes of contractors and subject-matter experts through LinkedIn Recruiter, job boards, referrals, talent communities and existing talent pools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screen and vet candidates quickly against project requirements, including skills assessments where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match and assign contractors to the right engagements, balancing skills, availability and client priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move contractors from offer through contracting, onboarding and training to their first billed hour, clearing blockers along the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track every contractor&#39;s path to billing and follow up quickly with anyone who stalls between acceptance and active work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redeploy contractors as projects ramp up, wind down or change scope to keep utilization high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-prioritize daily as urgent client needs open, working alongside the Sr. Manager, Staffing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the ATS and staffing trackers accurate and report weekly on fill rate, time-to-staff, time-to-first-billed-hour and utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of recruiting or staffing experience, including meaningful time in a staffing agency with a track record of meeting fill, placement and billable-hours targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in high-volume contract or contingent staffing, filling dozens of seats at once while keeping quality high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of urgency: you&#39;re energized by tight deadlines and can get qualified contractors from first contact to working in days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced sourcing skills, including Boolean search, LinkedIn Recruiter and creative channels for niche or hard-to-find skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing contractor onboarding, including contracts, compliance and readiness, in partnership with operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working directly with delivery teams and client stakeholders, and pushing back when needed to keep staffing on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on expertise with an ATS or staffing system (e.g., Greenhouse, Bullhorn, Workday, iCIMS) and strong spreadsheet skills for tracking pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment with confidential candidate, rate and client information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s In It For You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Invisible is committed to fair and competitive pay for our contractors, ensuring that rates reflect both market conditions and the value each contractor brings. Our contractor rate structure accounts for regional differences in cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a contractor, you will not be eligible for Invisible’s employee benefits, bonus, or equity programs. Final rates are determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, and overall market conditions. Additional details on rate, contract duration, and terms will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bonus and equity is included in all full-time, non commission offers. Final compensation is determined by a combination of factors, including location, job-related experience, skills, knowledge, internal pay equity, and overall market conditions. Because of this, every offer is unique. Additional details on total compensation and benefits will be discussed during the hiring process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can find more information about our geographic pay tiers&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://invisibletech.ai/compensation-and-pay-tiers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; During the interview process, your Invisible Talent Acquisition Partner will confirm which tier applies to your location. For candidates outside the U.S., compensation is adjusted to reflect local market conditions and cost of living.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It&#39;s Like to Work at Invisible:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Invisible, we’re not just redefining work—we’re reinventing it. We operate at the intersection of advanced AI and human ingenuity, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to unlock productivity and scale. Ownership is at the core of everything we do. Here, you won’t just execute tasks—you’ll build, innovate, and shape the future alongside world-class clients pushing the boundaries of AI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We expect bold ideas, relentless drive, and the ability to turn ambiguity into opportunity. The pace is fast, the challenges are big, and the growth is unmatched. We’re not for everyone, and we’re okay with that. If you’re looking for predictable routines, this isn’t the place for you. But if you’re driven to create, thrive in dynamic environments, and want a front-row seat to the AI revolution, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(85, 85, 85);&quot;&gt;Invisible is a hybrid organization with offices and team members located around the world. While some roles may offer remote flexibility, most positions involve in-office collaboration and are tied to specific locations. Any location-based requirements or hybrid expectations will be communicated by our Talent Acquisition team during the recruiting process.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;AI Interviewing Guidelines:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Our hiring team thoughtfully uses AI to support an efficient, engaging, and inclusive interview process. Since AI can also be a helpful tool for candidates, we&#39;ve outlined expectations for using it ethically throughout your interview journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(35, 111, 161);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.invisible.co/ai-interview-guidelines&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Click here to learn more about how we use AI and our guidelines for candidates.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
