&lt;h4&gt;About Cast AI&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cast AI is an automation platform that operates cloud-native and AI infrastructure at scale. By embedding autonomous decision-making directly into Kubernetes and cloud environments, Cast AI continuously optimizes performance, reliability, and efficiency in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cast AI also recently launched Kimchi, an open-source AI inference platform built for teams running serious agentic coding workloads. We&#39;re building the harness, the routing, and the infrastructure layer that makes running your own AI coding stack possible - and affordable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re trusted in our core business and early and moving fast with our Kimchi Coding platform, and the cloud native &amp;amp; developer communities are central to how we grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;United States (ideally West Coast, or willing to travel to the West Coast as needed).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build things publicly with the Cast AI suite of products - Core, GPU Optimization, Database Optimization (DBO), and Kimchi - tutorials, demos, integrations - that show developers how to solve real problems. Think live build logs, OSS integrations, or benchmarks you&#39;d want to read yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the voice of the the developer community: Discord, GitHub discussions, Reddit, HN - be present where developers are already talking about the problems we solve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the structured feedback loop between our diversity of users &amp;nbsp; and the&amp;nbsp; product - synthesize what you&#39;re hearing into actionable signals for the product team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write technical content that ranks and spreads: setup guides, benchmark breakdowns, comparison posts, integration walkthroughs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speak at conferences, meetups and run workshops - representing Cast AI core products &amp;amp; Kimchi as a technical peer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where new users get stuck and advocate hard for fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Cast AI’s voice across practitioner&amp;nbsp; communities (devs, DevOps, CNCF, AI, platform/SRE) - what we stand for, what we say when there is trending news in the market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built real software and can talk about it credibly - ideally you&#39;ve used Kubernetes and peripheral CNCF ecosystem tooling, as well as agentic coding tools and have opinions about them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a strong technical writer - you can explain complex things clearly and make them resonate with the developer audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable being the public face of a technical product: blog posts, talks, live demos, community threads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Huge plus: You&#39;d have tested and found problems Cast AI &amp;amp; Kimchi solve interesting -&amp;nbsp; before this job posting even existed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: you&#39;ve worked in or around Kubernetes, LLM inference, or developer tooling&lt;/li&gt;
