&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cast AI Database Optimizer (DBO) helps organizations improve database performance while reducing infrastructure&amp;nbsp;cost and operational effort. It combines autonomous query caching, connection pooling, AI-driven query rewriting, and&amp;nbsp;automated performance tuning for PostgreSQL and MySQL environments. Instead of stopping at recommendations&amp;nbsp;that engineering teams must implement themselves, DBO takes tuning actions automatically. It works with self-hosted,&amp;nbsp;cloud-hosted, and managed databases and does not require application code changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Founding Account Executive to develop and close new business for DBO as we turn early customer validation into a repeatable commercial motion. You will own the complete sales cycle: creating and converting pipeline, leading technical discovery and standard product demonstrations, coordinating proofs of concept, building the business case, and negotiating and closing new customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual-contributor role with unusual influence. You will work directly with Cast AI&#39;s founders and DBO Product and Engineering leaders to refine our ideal customer profile, sharpen our positioning, and turn customer learning into a scalable sales playbook. As the team grows, there will be opportunities to take on broader scope and help shape how the commercial organization develops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our primary focus is net-new customer acquisition in North America. The target market includes upper mid-market and emerging-enterprise organizations with meaningful database scale, as well as fast-growing cloud-native companies that offer faster adoption and land-and-expand potential. You will be supported by product marketing, inbound demand generation, and AI-assisted lead nurture. Cast AI will also bring the right Product and Engineering resources into&amp;nbsp;discovery and qualified proofs of concept, giving you strong technical support while you remain accountable for the&amp;nbsp;customer relationship and commercial process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success will be measured through new annual recurring revenue, net-new customers, qualified pipeline,&amp;nbsp;referenceable wins, forecast quality, and evidence that the DBO sales motion is becoming repeatable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five or more years of quota-carrying B2B technology sales experience, including enterprise or upper mid-market customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consistent record of meeting or exceeding new-business targets and winning net-new logos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling database, DBaaS, caching, data infrastructure, database observability, or application-performance solutions to technical organizations. Adjacent infrastructure experience may qualify when it includes repeated sales to DBAs or database-owning engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of PostgreSQL or MySQL and familiarity with concepts such as query performance, query optimization, caching, connection pooling, read replicas, and automated database tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading initial technical discovery and standard product demonstrations, with good judgment about when to involve Product or Engineering specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explore a customer&#39;s architecture, connect technical pain to business value, and recognize when Product or Engineering should join a deeper discussion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running time-bound technical evaluations or proofs of concept in partnership with customer and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create pipeline through focused outbound activity in addition to converting company-generated demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating multi-threaded sales involving DBAs, engineers, engineering leadership, security, procurement, and executive buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong qualification, pipeline management, and forecasting discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating without a mature playbook and a demonstrated bias toward action, ownership, and learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% for customer meetings, industry events, and periodic collaboration with our European Product and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a database platform, DBaaS, caching, database-performance, or observability company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of closing initial lands in the $50,000-$100,000 ARR range and expanding them over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building an early sales motion for a new product or category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency in relational databases and cloud infrastructure without losing focus on business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling effectively in a 60-90-day evaluation cycle that includes a proof of concept.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using customer and deal evidence to influence product strategy, messaging, and go-to-market execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full DBO sales cycle, from targeted prospecting and sales-ready inbound opportunities through discovery, demonstration, proof of concept, negotiation, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a meaningful portion of your pipeline through focused outbound activity while converting demand created through organic search, paid programs, events, partnerships, and AI-assisted nurture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead credible discovery with DBAs, application and platform engineers, FinOps teams, and engineering leaders to understand database cost, latency, scale, reliability, and operational challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver standard DBO product demonstrations independently and explain how autonomous caching, connection pooling, AI-driven query rewriting, and automated tuning apply to a customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define a clear value hypothesis, entry criteria, measurable success criteria, and mutual action plan before beginning a proof of concept.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering throughout discovery and qualified proofs of concept, bringing the right technical expertise into architecture, security, compatibility, and performance discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate technical findings into quantified business cases for engineering leaders and executive buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop champions and multi-thread relationships across technical, economic, security, procurement, and executive stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain disciplined opportunity qualification, pipeline management, and forecasting, and provide clear commercial insights to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture customer feedback, objections, competitive patterns, and win/loss insights to improve the product, positioning, and sales playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Cast AI at selected database, cloud-native, and infrastructure conferences and customer events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-powered workflows to improve account research, preparation, follow-up, pipeline analysis, and selling effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
